  "equipment_type": "Room sensor / transmitter",
  "applies_to": "Produal RXX-BAC wall sensors: RCD-BAC (CO2 and temperature, optional humidity), RRH-BAC (temperature and humidity), RTE-BAC (temperature) and RLL-BAC (light level and occupancy), with 0-10 V outputs, digital inputs and optional push buttons.",
  "summary": "The RXX-BAC sensors are wall room sensors with a built-in BACnet MS/TP interface, three 0-10 V outputs, resistive and digital inputs and two triac outputs; they can also run simple control loops. All four models use one fixed object map: sensor AIs, Y1-Y3 AOs, setpoint and pulse-count AVs, input and push-button BIs, output and LED BOs, and an alarm-level MSI. Objects for sensors a model does not have are printed as Not Assigned. This list is the full RCD-BAC set.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Object names are the Object_Name defaults in the product sheet property tables; objects printed as Not Assigned or Not Applicable (including BO 7) are left out.",
    "Per model: RCD-BAC has every object listed. RRH-BAC has no CO2 objects (AI 5, AV 2) and names AI 3/4 \"RI1\"/\"RI2\". RTE-BAC also has no humidity objects (AI 2, AV 1). RLL-BAC has only AI 0, 1, 4 (RI2) and 6 and no AV 1, 2, 7 or 8.",
    "The RLL-BAC instance summary puts the backlight brightness at AV(7), but its property tables give AV(6), as on the other models.",
    "Access is inferred: AIs, BIs and the MSI read-only; AOs, AVs and BOs writable (the sheet lists a priority array for AVs and BOs).",
    "Temperatures follow the device unit setting (°C or °F). Push buttons 1-4 and their LEDs only exist with the push-button (SPB) options; set Push Button Mode to BMS to drive the LEDs.",
    "AI 5 is printed as \"C02 Sensor\" (with a zero). The RCD instance summary also calls AI 1 \"Calculated Setpoint\". Separate product sheets: PS 6041-RRH-BAC, PS 6041-RTE-BAC and PS 6041-RLL-BAC (all 10/2020)."
  ],
